302
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:12,840
Hey, Prez,

303
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,600
will you be okay?

304
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,260
I don't have an umbrella,

305
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:16,260
but I suppose

306
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:17,200
I'll be running home.

307
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,120
Isn't that a little

308
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,040
too daring of you?

309
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,000
Ah, what the heck.

310
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,720
I'll give up my spot

311
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,640
under Yamada's umbrella

312
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,380
for you, Prez.

313
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,280
Are you cool

314
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:25,960
with that, Yamada?

315
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:27,040
Either one of you

316
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:27,480
is fine.

317
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:27,940
Huh?

318
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:28,980
But I'd feel bad.

319
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:29,820
Why don't you two

320
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:30,260
just go?

321
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,300
Nah, how could I

322
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:31,960
put my own needs

323
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,080
over the head of a lady's?

324
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,460
In this way,

325
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,820
you can go home together

326
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,140
so you should pounce.

327
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:39,880
I don't need you

328
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:40,600
to look out for me

329
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,380
like that, you know?

330
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:42,960
Yamada will think

331
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,780
I'm a weirdo.

332
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:45,080
Don't you know

333
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:45,680
you'll never get

334
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:46,400
anywhere with him

335
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,160
unless you come off

336
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:47,960
as a little weird?

337
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,300
Especially you.

338
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,900
They can't settle it

339
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:55,580
because they're trying

340
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,140
to give it up

341
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:56,700
to each other?

342
00:11:58,640 --> 00:11:59,500
Maybe I'll just

343
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:00,420
give them my umbrella

344
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:01,580
and make a run for it.

345
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:04,100
Yamada?

346
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,080
Hmm?

347
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:06,780
Hey, uh...

348
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,460
on second thought

349
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:10,200
we could share

350
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:10,720
your umbrella

351
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,380
until we get

352
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,060
to the station

353
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:13,020
if that's cool.

354
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:15,180
Oh yeah.

355
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,680
I decided to try

356
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:17,320
that new game.

357
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:18,740
It's still in beta

358
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:19,280
right now

359
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,320
so it's pretty buggy.

360
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:21,660
But it looks like

361
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:22,680
it'll be really good.

362
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,480
Hurry up!

363
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:30,900
Just wait!

364
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,300
You're so slow, Saki.

365
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,260
My shoes are slippery.

366
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:36,680
Such bad weather.

367
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,680
Do you know that person?

368
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:39,660
Who?

369
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:40,960
Right there.

370
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,140
Because your eyes

371
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:42,960
were following her

372
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,300
when she ran by just now.

373
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,100
I don't know her.

374
00:12:47,100 --> 00:13:05,660
Uh, Tsubaki.

375
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:06,840
Here.

376
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:07,760
Please take this

377
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,740
for yourself after all.

378
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:14,260
Huh?

379
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:15,100
How come?

380
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,420
It would defeat the purpose

381
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,160
if you got wet.

382
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:17,900
So please.

383
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:18,500
But why?

384
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:19,460
What about you?

385
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:20,620
I'll make a run for it.

386
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,740
The station's right there.

387
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,360
Um...

388
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,580
Wait, I...

389
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:46,180
Wait!

390
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:48,100
Wait!

391
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,200
Please wait!

392
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:50,680
Yamada!

393
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:52,640
Stop!

394
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,180
Please!

395
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,700
I'm sorry.

396
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,300
My glasses...

397
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:05,300
I can't see.

398
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:21,040
They're broken.

399
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:21,360
They're broken.

400
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:25,260
Are you okay?

401
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:32,440
I like you.

402
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,400
What?

403
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:42,180
I like you.

404
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:42,220
I like you.

405
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:46,180
I like you.

406
00:14:46,180 --> 00:15:16,160
Sorry to put you on the spot.

407
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:16,780
I like you.

408
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:17,120
But...

409
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,540
But...

410
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,860
Please.

411
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,700
Just for today.

412
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,540
I want you to try

413
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,260
thinking of me.

414
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,160
It can just be for today.

415
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:33,620
Oh...

416
00:15:33,620 --> 00:15:52,360
What's the time?

417
00:15:52,360 --> 00:16:05,000
You know, it was raining really hard yesterday, huh?

418
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,020
It was so loud, it woke me up right out of my sleep.

419
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,680
And then, I couldn't sleep a wink after that.

420
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,800
You're not concentrating at all, are you, Runa?

421
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,120
Nope, not anymore.

422
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:20,400
Good work, studying so hard.

423
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:23,100
I brought you some donuts, so please have some, you two.

424
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:23,920
Donuts!

425
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:27,840
I really appreciate you taking time out of your own studies to help her, Yamada.

426
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:31,700
When we were looking for a tutor, Runa insisted she didn't want anyone but you.

427
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,720
She must really adore you.

428
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:38,560
But I have to say, seeing the two of you together like this, you make such a nice couple.

429
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:39,800
Isn't that right, son?

430
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:41,280
You're getting pretty bold there, Mom.

431
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,040
Not hiding your ambitions even a little.

432
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,000
What do you mean?

433
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,120
Who knows?

434
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:49,560
All I'm saying is that those two would make quite the sweet couple, if you say so, Mom.

435
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,060
Do you know what they're talking about?

436
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:51,940
No clue.

437
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,200
Must be some kind of joke, maybe?

438
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,400
By the way, Akito, that reminds me.

439
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,800
Someone confessed to you yesterday, didn't they?

440
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,540
How did you know?

441
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:05,560
I know everything, okay?

442
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:08,280
So Akanechi really confessed, huh?

443
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:09,920
That girl's amazing.

444
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,800
So, what'd you do?

445
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:12,720
How'd you respond?

446
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,800
That's none of your concern.

447
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:15,620
It is, though.

448
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:16,520
It is, huh?

449
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,280
I'm still thinking.

450
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,580
Ah, is that so?

451
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,280
I was sure you were actually gonna go for it, though.

452
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:26,500
Huh.

453
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:28,180
Since you're so close.

454
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:28,980
Wow.

455
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:31,220
You really are vague, my guy.

456
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:35,320
You should give her your answer sooner than later and be clear about it.

457
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:38,780
Being suggestive with someone and then toying with them is the worst thing you could do.

458
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:42,140
I'd never do that.

459
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:46,560
Stupid Eita made Yamada mad again.

460
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,400
I'm sorry, Akun.

461
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,160
Take these donuts.

462
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,360
Please don't be mad.

463
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,740
These donuts are runes.

464
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:56,320
The number you are trying to reach is out of signal range or has been turned off.

465
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:57,960
Please hang up and try again.

466
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:00,660
Oh.

467
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:02,180
Akane.

468
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,040
Akane.

469
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,180
Look who's waiting outside.

470
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:07,880
Hey, Yamada!

471
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,500
What are you doing here?

472
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:14,260
It's kinda unusual for you to stop by our store.

473
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:15,960
Aren't you supposed to be working?

474
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,200
I asked to do some outside work.

475
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:20,220
Now then, have you come to see me?

476
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,680
I'm just kidding.

477
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:22,240
That's right.

478
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:22,680
Huh?

479
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,800
I did try calling you, but it didn't go through.

480
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:27,540
Oh, you did, huh?

481
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:28,540
Sorry about that.

482
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:31,900
My battery was already down to 3% when I left my apartment.

483
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:32,980
That's okay.

484
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:37,800
I just thought if I could see you in person, I could apologize for yesterday.

485
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,080
No.

486
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:40,360
Oh.

487
00:18:42,060 --> 00:18:43,400
I don't mind at all.

488
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,540
It wasn't really important anyway.

489
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:49,740
And come to think of it, I've already talked to Momo about it, so...

490
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:52,160
I've pretty much gotten it off my chest, I guess.

491
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,120
But never mind that.

492
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,300
You seem a little down today.

493
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:57,320
What's wrong?

494
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,240
Do I?

495
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,080
I'm feeling pretty normal.

496
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:01,940
Huh?

497
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:03,560
You're so not like you.

498
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:04,820
Your voice has no energy.

499
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,120
Well, that's always the case.

500
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,780
You're also not very talkative.

501
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:09,440
I guess you never are, though.

502
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,380
You're usually like this.

503
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,960
But today, you're like this.

504
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:13,480
Hmm?

505
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:13,660
Hmm?

506
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:25,220
I guess I've been a little busy, so maybe I'm tired.

507
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,420
Studying for entrance exams must be draining.

508
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:28,740
That's tough.

509
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:31,760
His problems are on a whole different planet than mine.

510
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:32,780
I see.

511
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:37,920
Oh, hey, I forgot to tell you.

512
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,040
I recently got some new gear in FOS.

513
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:45,060
I've been dying to brag about it to you, but you never seem to log in these days.

514
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,620
I got myself a sweet new sword.

515
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,000
What kind of sword?

516
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:50,540
What kind?

517
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,560
Meaning...

518
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:55,080
You know, like the weapon rank or type.

519
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,940
Uh, let's see.

520
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,140
Give me your hand.

521
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:02,020
Is that permanent?

522
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:02,980
Give me your hand.

523
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:06,940
Those bosses sure drop some great items, don't they?

524
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:11,360
I've been wondering why you're always raiding bosses, but I think I finally get it now.

525
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:13,760
Well, yeah, though the odds of a drop are slim.

526
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:14,580
I know, right?

527
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:18,480
So when a decent item does end up dropping, it makes you feel outrageously happy.

528
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:19,600
It's exhilarating.

529
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:23,920
I don't know what's going on, but it will pass.

530
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:27,700
Then you can go back to being your mysterious self.

531
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,700
So that's how I look to people.

532
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:42,920
I'm usually quiet because I'm scared I'll say the wrong thing, so I say nothing.

533
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:47,360
I'm not very good at reading into other people's feelings.

534
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:51,040
And most of the time, their jokes go right over my head.

535
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:53,500
I know that I'm boring.

536
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:55,360
It's obvious.

537
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,000
Hmm.

538
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:07,980
If you ask me, you know how you sometimes set me straight in that astute way of yours?

539
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:10,220
I really like that.

540
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:15,100
And when you're with us, you don't say much, but I know you're looking out for everyone.

541
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:19,400
Also, I know you always try to help people out if they're in trouble.

542
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:22,740
Because you've already done that for me so many times.

543
00:21:23,780 --> 00:21:25,540
And you're not boring at all.

544
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,180
Like I said, you're fun.

545
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:28,920
Trust me on that.

546
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,060
I mean it.

547
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,440
Okay?

548
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,880
When I wake up, I let out a sigh.

549
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:11,400
Somewhere along the way, that became a habit of mine.

550
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:17,000
I was so sure.

551
00:23:17,940 --> 00:23:20,340
Yukari, you're going out at this hour?

552
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:23,380
Just for a bit. I'm supposed to meet up with a friend.

553
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:26,120
Well, come home as soon as you can, okay?

554
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:26,740
Yeah.

555
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:32,060
That love was supposed to be more fun than this.

556
00:23:33,000 --> 00:24:02,980
Thank you.

